# Offline and sync

Local-first: read IndexedDB first, then merge remote `log_entries` when cloud is reachable. Writes go to IndexedDB immediately; `useSyncQueue` ships them when online.

`useOffline().isOnline` is **Supabase reachability** (auth health probe), not `navigator.onLine`. Do not process the sync queue unless that flag is true. Keep the offline session snapshot (`cachedSupabaseSession`); do not treat a missing SDK session as logout while offline.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
if (navigator.onLine) await processQueue()

// ✅ GOOD
const { isOnline } = useOffline()
if (isOnline.value) await processQueue({ silent: true })
```

Offline is a normal cockpit state. Do not leave a persistent “Offline” banner that never clears. Sync status (iOS banner, pull-to-sync) should be brief and dismissible.

Known gap: first visit with **empty IndexedDB and no network** shows an empty logbook. Do not “fix” that by blocking the UI on cloud. Full offline requires a prior successful sync on that device.
